     "sha256": "632b5059fa9c17b4588eee6acbefa67411d693b997e71e003f20a31271230318",
     "text": "**Date:** 2026-10-17. **Status:** design only. **Branch:** master. **Program:** [Adaptive Computation and Control](https://github.com/jehalladay/FiberOpticsResearch/tree/main/docs/research/foa/programs/adaptive-computation-and-control-2026-10-17). **Work packages:** AC-01, AC-06, AC-15."
    },
    {
     "line": 35,
     "sha256": "bc57b43b55006462f42a08a9f8fe770fdd6547c58ac375f8bbd1df7307d0f419",
     "text": "ReactiveQuerySDK was created as a separate pure maintained evidence/query engine (https://github.com/jehalladay/ReactiveQuerySDK/tree/main/docs/program). It does not change ReactiveInferenceSDK's provider-neutral model execution, capability, cancellation and token/usage authority. A query result can be *conditioning data* in a context/agent request, but query recomputation or a change from UNKNOWN to TRUE never directly calls a model from ReactiveInferenceSDK."
    },
    {
     "line": 37,
     "sha256": "88ff01a3e58c067782c7bae4f6612a72b4ab37b600f607c70a2c7d5aac83fc14",
     "text": "Keep the existing source/gen/capability/usage receipts for actual admitted inference. Speculative inference remains disabled by default; query evidence proof is not a license for a speculative model operation. If a host includes QueryView source witness in model context basis, the existing model request identifier/receipt should retain it as typed provenance, without inventing a query engine inside the inference SDK."
    },
    {
     "line": 39,
     "sha256": "7fda4bd34ab435bb2e8747f4f9193073a053d3ba6b3dc76076fafe8c8690c726",
     "text": "Acceptance INF-RQ1 ordinary inference API import/run unaffected without QuerySDK, INF-RQ2 query-view changes alone produce no network calls, INF-RQ3 exact provider usage/cancel disposition preserved, INF-RQ4 generation-fenced inferences cannot publish stale output into newer evidence snapshot, INF-RQ5 DevTools and QuerySDK remain optional dependencies and local Forge/installed source gates remain binding."
    }
   ]
  },
